.TH TONE 2
.SH NAME
tone: init, snd, beep, stop, play \- simple tones and scored melodies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "tone.m";
tone := load Tone Tone->PATH;

Rate: con 22050;

init: fn(): string;
snd:  fn(freq: int);
beep: fn(freq, duration_ms: int);
stop: fn();
play: fn(score: string): string;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tone
.RB ( /dis/lib/tone.dis )
generates simple monophonic audio for Inferno applications.
It writes PCM to the device described in
.IR audio (3)
at
.B Tone->Rate
samples per second (22050 Hz), matching the usual emulator default.
Applications use it for short beeps and for compact melody strings.
.PP
.B Init
opens the audio device.
It returns
.B nil
on success, or a diagnostic string if audio is unavailable.
Callers that treat sound as optional (most TempleOS games) simply leave a
flag clear when
.B init
fails.
.PP
.B Snd
starts a continuous square-ish tone at
.I freq
Hertz.
A frequency of
.B 0
silences output (equivalent to turning the PC speaker off).
.B Beep
plays
.I freq
for
.I duration_ms
milliseconds and then stops.
If
.I duration_ms
is less than or equal to zero, the tone continues until
.B stop
is called.
.B Stop
silences immediately.
.PP
.B Play
interprets a compact score string.
Digits set the current octave (programs typically use 4 through 6).
The letters
.BR w ,
.BR h ,
.BR q ,
.BR e ,
and
.B s
select whole, half, quarter, eighth, and sixteenth durations.
Notes are
.B A
through
.BR G ,
with
.B #
and
.B b
accidentals;
.B R
is a rest.
An example used by several demos is
.BR 6hEqDC5B6CDhE .
.B Play
blocks while notes are emitted and returns
.B nil
or an error string.
.PP
.IR Asciiorgan (1)
maps typed keys to
.BR beep .
.IR Ohgreat (1)
and
.IR psalmody (1)
drive
.BR play .
Many games spawn a small loop that repeatedly
.B play s
background phrases while a pause flag is clear.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
	if(tone->init() == nil){
		tone->beep(880, 100);
		tone->play("5qCEqG");
		tone->stop();
	}
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/tone.b
.br
.B /module/tone.m
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR audio (3),
.IR asciiorgan (1),
.IR ohgreat (1),
.IR psalmody (1),
.IR temple (1)
.SH BUGS
Only one voice is available.
